			<div class="content" id="post-content-4204649">
									

<p>This one started off as a single-line concept in my head, &quot;rock paper fhtagn&quot;, and went through a couple of iterations before I settled on this one.</p>
<p>Yes, the USA Rock Paper Scissors League was a real thing. Yes, it had commentary, it was on ESPN. Yes, the commentary was almost exactly like this.</p>
<p>Thanks to Rounderhouse, TheMightyMcB, Lazar, weryllium, MaliceAF, Hippo and Tufto for reading the draft of this!</p>
<p>Check out more of my stuff <a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/mortos-author-page" target="_blank">here!</a></p>
<p>Image creds:<br />
Image is an edited composite of 2 other images -<br />
<a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Rock,_Paper,_Scissors#/media/File:Mushi-ken_(%E8%99%AB%E6%8B%B3),_Japanese_rock-paper-scissors_variant,_from_the_Kensarae_sumai_zue_(1809).jpg">https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Rock,_Paper,_Scissors#/media/File:Mushi-ken_(%E8%99%AB%E6%8B%B3),_Japanese_rock-paper-scissors_variant,_from_the_Kensarae_sumai_zue_(1809).jpg</a></p>
<p><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hagfish#/media/File:NIE_1905_Hagfish_-_Myxine_glutinosa.jpg">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hagfish#/media/File:NIE_1905_Hagfish_-_Myxine_glutinosa.jpg</a></p>

